{"agent":"impl-sw-score","data":{"by":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"`queue_ref_s` is validated with `_count`, so `queue_ref_s = 0` is accepted. The knob is a reference time for the queue term (“seconds … at which the queue term reaches one”), which implies a positive normalization time; with zero, a score implementation that computes the linear ramp as `waited_s / queue_ref_s` raises `ZeroDivisionError`, and even if guarded the documented ramp semantics are lost. The sibling reference knobs `cost_ref_usd` and `rework_ref` correctly enforce `> 0`, while this one does not.","digest":"415780613e139e6f","location":"ddflow/config_sections/swarm.py:81","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/config_sections/swarm.py:81"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"The global `max_lanes` cap counts distinct `Live.item` IDs, not live leases. If an item has multiple live hedges, `world.live` can contain several entries with the same item ID, and `{lv.item for lv in world.live}` collapses them. Given `w.max_lanes = 2` and `world.live = (Live(\"A\", globs=(), family=\"x\"), Live(\"A\", globs=(), family=\"y\"))`, scheduling item `B` sees only one distinct live item, so `_state_refusals` emits no `swarm at max_lanes` refusal. `choose` can then dispatch `B`, producing three live leases while the global cap is 2. This is inconsistent with the per-family and per-lane caps, which count live leases, and defeats the global concurrency cap.","digest":"e66ed6342eb39709","location":"ddflow/services/swarm/score.py:_state_refusals","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/services/swarm/score.py:_state_refusals"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"`_terms` divides by `w.cost_ref_usd` and `w.rework_ref` without zero guards, while it explicitly guards `w.queue_ref_s`. If a zero reference reaches this pure function (for example, via a directly constructed `Weights` or a config validated only as non-negative), `evaluate` raises `ZeroDivisionError` instead of returning a refusal or neutral term. For instance, with `Lane(local=True)`, `est_cost` returns `0.0`; with `Weights(cost_ref_usd=0.0, ...)`, the line `cost_t = 1.0 - min(1.0, cost / w.cost_ref_usd)` raises even if the lane would otherwise be refused. Similarly, a ledger cell with `cell.items > 0` and `w.rework_ref = 0.0` raises at the rework division.","digest":"281d926c41a42cbf","location":"ddflow/services/swarm/score.py:_terms","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/swarm/score.py:_terms"},{"chunk":7,"detail":"The `_worlds` strategy builds `World` as `st.builds(World, done=..., live=...)`, but every other construction in the file supplies a `ledger` argument (`_world` does `World(ledger=L.Ledger(...), **kw)`). If `World.ledger` has no default—as the helper implies—Hypothesis will raise `TypeError: World.__init__() missing required argument 'ledger'` on the first property example, so `test_property_score_never_overrides_a_constraint_and_is_deterministic` never exercises the scheduler.","digest":"3cc080bd118d56ab","location":"tests/test_swarm_score.py:165","severity":"HIGH","title":"tests/test_swarm_score.py:165"}],"chunks_total":7,"coverage":"7/7 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":35650,"diff_sha":"ba60681600bff91bdf890095eaf710a4170a3e991ab09702e8e5923d4271af2e","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":659.3,"excluded_bytes":8507,"excluded_files":2,"excluded_paths":["README.md","tests/golden/__snapshots__/test_golden_outputs.ambr"],"family":"alibaba","findings":4,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","output_digest":"c09a1b7cad5064a8","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/SW-score.rubber_duck.qwen3.8-flash-next-fp8.20261030T155233Z-719e8cdd.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3,4,5,6,7],"reviewed_head":"3721bfca3f3dc4e6997301a056c0912d3c0e58a0","reviewed_paths":{"README.md":"100644 58b54b30f12647d0f07c6561d175a1170bef4bf3